<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea to make 6.29 bln won in loans to Mongolia.</title>
<headline>S.Korea to make 6.29 bln won in loans to Mongolia.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea has agreed to lend 6.29 billion won in soft loans to help finance thermal power plant construction projects in Mongolia, a foreign ministry statement said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 20-year loans have a five year grace period and carry a fixed annual interest of 3.0 percent.</p>
<p>The money is a part of South Korea's Economic Development Cooperation Fund (EDCF), set up in 1987 to help finance developing countries and to boost domestic companies' business expansion in the region.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
